Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f48240e9-4ecb-ed4b-8f50-fe6adfba00f2"],

Cell["\<\
1. Observe FirstOrder breakdown: In Lab 2A, increase Test RF Amp to 800 Hz \
and Duration T to 20 ms. Notice how FirstOrder error grows dramatically while \
Spectral stays ~10^-11.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6d476830-e5a3-fc47-a03a-9c5bc112ca18"],

Cell["\<\
2. Locate optimal FD step: Move log10(Step h) across [-8, -1]. Why does h = \
10^-8 lose precision at high RF amplitudes?\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3b367b41-d824-8741-9b5e-42ffee6e7d5c"],

Cell["\<\
3. Benchmark D = 16 scaling: In Lab 2B, set N = 4 spins (D = 16, M = 8 \
channels) and run Benchmark Kernels. Observe how channel-independent Spectral \
and StateVector outperform M-dependent BlockMatrixExp.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8460fae0-5b9f-214b-b05c-7f27fe6a470d"],

Cell["\<\
4. Try Method -> \"StateVector\" on UnitaryTarget in a scratch cell to verify \
SpinDynamica catches the incompatible kernel cleanly with \
OptimalControlProblem::badmethod.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3ced445f-0416-ef48-9faf-4b743a8fd4d5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a1282b5e-d37b-cf46-9c1a-f6c7c0d180a7"],

Cell["\<\
Exact eigensystem Sinc Fr\[EAcute]chet derivatives evaluate all M channels in \
a single spectral decomposition without eigenvalue degeneracy thresholds, \
agreeing with BlockMatrixExp and StateVector to machine precision. Setting \
FrequencyUnits and ControlUnits consistently prevents 2*Pi scaling errors.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13ac45b8-5124-b04a-a8ec-788d4d24b342"],

